  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Dribbling – 2v2 with four goals",
  "description": "Play 2v2 on a pitch of about 20 × 10 metres with two small goals at each end. Both teams may score in all four goals. Split a normal court across its width, so each pitch is long enough to dribble and attack the space behind the opponents. The diagram shows two pitches, one in each half, and is not to scale.\n\nIf you don't have enough goals, use cones. If you use full-size goals without goalkeepers, the defenders have to press much harder; an extra rule can then be that you may not shoot while standing in front of an opponent with the goal behind them – you have to dribble past first.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Dribble into the free space – speed up once you are past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "If one goal is closed off, change direction and go for another."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: when is it hard to defend? Talk it through with the players."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When can you let go with one hand on the stick to reach further?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
